From 71ae934676df880debba5e0bc99283e8b6700d9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:26:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): warn when a 2D Pocket tool cannot fit, refuse a
 too-narrow Slot edit

A 2D Pocket's MCP replies (add_operation, edit_operation, set_tool,
set_operation_area) now carry a named warning when the tool has no
centre position in the region that Generate cuts. The advice builds
that region the way Generate does (collect_job, region_for_job, the
area controls) and applies the generator's own predicate, now public
as machining2d::pocket_tool_fits. It does not run where it cannot
build the same region (tilt, WCS yaw, sketch source, rest machining).

EditOperationParams refuses a plain Slot edit of width or
stock_to_leave that leaves the mounted tool too wide, with the #3475
sentence.

Fixes #3631

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
